I had a look at the contribution. It should be fine. However, there are a few code style issues you must fix before we can add the code.
The following values must be declared final in WriterController
203         Class<?> strategyClass = Class.forName(strategyName);
215        Class<?> strategyClass = Class.forName(strategyName);

39 and 40 in WriterController refer to unused imports.

Missing whitespace before =.
115  final TakeStrategy takeStrategy= newTakeStrategy(takeStrategyFqn);

You can fix these things all together with setting up Eclipse following the steps in our setup instructions. In case you use some other IDE, you most likely can set the same parameter there. Also please record such setup efforts, as we could add them to our documentation for others.

https://kieker-monitoring.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/DEV/pages/24215585/Kieker+Coding+Conventions+in+Eclipse

I used the previous PR #48 as a base for this PR as I had no control over the original one. This was my try to integrate the Zuul support, but as I had no deep insight into the details and several issues throughout the build, it did not succeed. 
We could either ask the original author @ChristianStier whether he would be interested in updating his PR for the current version, try to fix it ourselves, or just drop it if nobody can invest time in fixing it.

@rju You are right, the base version of the PR is 1.13 and would need to be updated accordingly.

